course: dictionary
lesson: 8256
title: Rice: a food and a plant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «Three grains feed much of humanity: rice, wheat and maize.» Here rice is a food, one of the grains we eat.
explain: Rice can also mean the plant itself, a kind of grass that grows in wet fields called paddies. «Farmers in hilly places cut steps called terraces into the slopes, so the flat steps hold water» is about growing crops on land, so rice here means the plant.
explain: Sometimes rice is used to compare things. «At the vet's, a microchip about the size of a grain of rice slides under the skin» uses rice to show how small the microchip is. Always ask: which meaning fits in this sentence?
fact: Rice is a food made of small white or brown grains.
fact: Rice is also the plant itself, a kind of grass that grows in wet fields called paddies.
fact: «Rice, wheat and maize are the most important crops in the world.»
fact: Rice grows mostly in Asia, in fields that are flooded with water.
fact: «Chopsticks are never stuck upright in rice» because in some Asian cultures that looks like a funeral custom.
exercise: «Three grains feed much of humanity: rice, wheat and maize.» In this sentence, what is rice? | A loud noise | *A food made of small grains | A kind of animal | A type of cloud
exercise: Paddies are the wet fields where rice grows. What are paddies? | *Wet fields where rice grows | Steep hills covered in snow | Shops that sell grain | Dry deserts with cactus plants
exercise: «At the vet's, a microchip about the size of a grain of rice slides under the skin.» What is rice being used to show? | That the puppy is hungry | That the vet likes cooking | *How small the microchip is | How much the microchip costs
test: Mia says, «Rice is a grass that grows in the paddy field.» Which meaning of rice does she use? | A bag in the shop | A food for dinner | *The plant itself | A grain of sand
test: «Chopsticks are never stuck upright in rice, and it is fine to ask for a fork.» What does this sentence suggest? | *Sticking chopsticks upright can look like a funeral custom in some Asian cultures | Rice is a fish that lives in water | Chopsticks are made of rice | Forks are always rude to use
exam: Rice grows in flooded fields. What is the name for these fields? | slopes | *paddies | terraces | microchips
